ue of the county&rsquo;s 7 grids in Worth County shows October to November and November to December each came in under 90% of normal in 38 of 75 years since 1951. In 2025 the middle got 33% of normal in September to October and 45% in October to November. So far in 2026 it ran 40% of normal in March to April, then 190% in May to June. Every grid had its driest year in 1954, with grid 13986 at 50% of normal.</p>"}
